(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) Tj
T*
(PAGE 95: SINUSITIS \(ACUTE AND CHRONIC RHINOSINUSITIS\)) Tj
T*
(Section: Otolaryngology, Rhinology & Upper Airway Health) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition and Clinical Overview: Sinusitis is inflammation of the mucosal lining) Tj
T*
(of the paranasal sinuses and nasal cavity, characterized by nasal congestion,) Tj
T*
(facial pressure, and purulent discharge.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Is the Reason \(Underlying Etiology & Mechanisms\): Obstruction of the sinus) Tj
T*
(ostia following a viral cold, mucosal edema, and impaired ciliary clearance allow) Tj
T*
(mucus stagnation and secondary bacterial infection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate Action Plan \(What to Do Right Now for Relief\): Perform nasal saline) Tj
T*
(irrigations using a neti pot with sterile water, inhale warm steam from a bowl or) Tj
T*
(shower, apply warm face compresses, and stay hydrated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proper Plan: How to Cure & Prevent \(Long-Term Management\): Use intranasal) Tj
T*
(corticosteroid sprays; viral sinusitis resolves in 7-10 days; bacterial sinusitis) Tj
T*
(\(symptoms >10 days or 'double-sickening'\) requires amoxicillin-clavulanate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Red-Flag Warning Signs \(When to Seek Emergency Care\): Seek emergency care for) Tj
T*
(swelling or redness around the eye, vision changes, severe frontal headache with) Tj
T*
(fever, or stiff neck.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
