T*
(PAGE 97: SYSTEMIC LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS \(SLE\) AND AUTOIMMUNITY) Tj
T*
(Section: Rheumatology, Autoimmune Connective Tissue Disease) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition and Clinical Overview: Systemic lupus erythematosus is a multisystem) Tj
T*
(autoimmune connective tissue disease characterized by antibodies against nuclear) Tj
T*
(antigens \(ANA\) and immune-complex deposition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Is the Reason \(Underlying Etiology & Mechanisms\): Defective clearance of) Tj
T*
(apoptotic debris exposes nuclear antigens to autoantibodies, forming immune) Tj
T*
(complexes that deposit in kidneys, skin, joints, and serosa.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate Action Plan \(What to Do Right Now for Relief\): Avoid direct sunlight and) Tj
T*
(UV exposure \(wear sun-protective clothing and SPF 50+ sunscreen\), get plenty of) Tj
T*
(restorative rest, and manage emotional stress.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proper Plan: How to Cure & Prevent \(Long-Term Management\): Consult a) Tj
T*
(rheumatologist for regular disease monitoring; first-line therapy is) Tj
T*
(hydroxychloroquine, along with targeted immunosuppressants and kidney function) Tj
T*
(surveillance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Red-Flag Warning Signs \(When to Seek Emergency Care\): Seek emergency care for) Tj
T*
(chest pain worse with breathing \(pericarditis/pleuritis\), shortness of breath, new) Tj
T*
(confusion, or rapidly swelling legs with foamy urine.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
