T*
(PAGE 98: TENDONITIS \(ACHILLES, PATELLAR AND BICIPITAL\)) Tj
T*
(Section: Sports Medicine, Physical Therapy & Tendinopathy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition and Clinical Overview: Tendonitis is acute inflammation and micro-) Tj
T*
(injury of a tendon, the fibrous connective tissue structure that anchors muscle to) Tj
T*
(bone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Is the Reason \(Underlying Etiology & Mechanisms\): Repetitive mechanical) Tj
T*
(overload, abrupt increases in training volume, improper biomechanics, and) Tj
T*
(inadequate recovery create micro-tears in collagen fibers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate Action Plan \(What to Do Right Now for Relief\): Rest from aggravating) Tj
T*
(repetitive movements, apply ice packs wrapped in a towel for 15 minutes 3 times) Tj
T*
(daily, and use a supportive brace or wrap.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proper Plan: How to Cure & Prevent \(Long-Term Management\): Perform gentle) Tj
T*
(eccentric strengthening exercises \(such as heel drops for Achilles\), avoid) Tj
T*
(aggressive stretching of the inflamed tendon, and pursue physical therapy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Red-Flag Warning Signs \(When to Seek Emergency Care\): Seek urgent orthopedic) Tj
T*
(evaluation for a sudden loud 'pop' or snap accompanied by immediate severe pain) Tj
T*
(and inability to move the limb \(tendon rupture\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
