(PAGE 99: TONSILLITIS, PERITONSILLAR ABSCESS AND PHARYNGEAL HEALTH) Tj
T*
(Section: Otolaryngology, Infectious Diseases & Airway Safety) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition and Clinical Overview: Tonsillitis is acute infection and inflammatory) Tj
T*
(swelling of the palatine tonsils, accompanied by sore throat, fever, and painful) Tj
T*
(swallowing \(odynophagia\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Is the Reason \(Underlying Etiology & Mechanisms\): Respiratory viruses or) Tj
T*
(Group A Streptococcus bacteria infect tonsillar crypts, triggering tonsillar) Tj
T*
(erythema, exudates, and jugulodigastric lymphadenopathy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate Action Plan \(What to Do Right Now for Relief\): Gargle with warm salt) Tj
T*
(water every 2-3 hours, drink cool soothing liquids or fruit smoothies, use throat) Tj
T*
(lozenges, and take acetaminophen or ibuprofen for pain.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proper Plan: How to Cure & Prevent \(Long-Term Management\): Consult a healthcare) Tj
T*
(provider for throat swab testing; confirmed strep requires antibiotics; recurrent) Tj
T*
(severe episodes may warrant tonsillectomy consultation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Red-Flag Warning Signs \(When to Seek Emergency Care\): Seek emergency care) Tj
T*
(immediately for difficulty breathing, drooling, inability to swallow liquids, or) Tj
T*
(severe unilateral throat swelling with a deviated uvula \(peritonsillar abscess\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
