T*
(PAGE 100: ULCERATIVE COLITIS AND MUCOSAL COLONIC REMISSION) Tj
T*
(Section: Gastroenterology, Colorectal Surgery & IBD Care) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition and Clinical Overview: Ulcerative colitis is a chronic inflammatory) Tj
T*
(bowel disease causing continuous, superficial mucosal inflammation and ulcerations) Tj
T*
(extending proximally from the rectum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Is the Reason \(Underlying Etiology & Mechanisms\): Dysregulated colonic) Tj
T*
(mucosal immune response against commensal gut microbiota in genetically) Tj
T*
(predisposed individuals, causing crypt abscesses and friability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate Action Plan \(What to Do Right Now for Relief\): Rest, drink oral) Tj
T*
(rehydration fluids with electrolytes, eat small bland meals \(bananas, white rice\),) Tj
T*
(and avoid spicy, high-fat, or high-fiber foods during acute flares.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proper Plan: How to Cure & Prevent \(Long-Term Management\): Consult a) Tj
T*
(gastroenterologist for colonoscopy staging and long-term maintenance therapy \(oral) Tj
T*
(5-ASAs like mesalamine, biologics, or JAK inhibitors\), with annual colon cancer) Tj
T*
(screening.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Red-Flag Warning Signs \(When to Seek Emergency Care\): Seek emergency medical) Tj
T*
(evaluation for heavy rectal bleeding, high fever, severe abdominal pain, or rapid) Tj
T*
(abdominal distension with tachycardia \(toxic megacolon\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
